## Discord Embed Field Limits

**CRITICAL**: Discord embed field values have a hard limit of 1024 characters. When adding potentially long text to embeds (e.g., lists of items, inventory contents), always use the `addLongField()` utility function from `src/app/bot/utils/embed-helpers.ts`.

**Never** directly call `embed.addFields()` with user-generated or dynamically-sized content that could exceed 1024 characters. This will cause runtime validation errors.

**Example:**
```typescript
import { addLongField } from "../../utils/embed-helpers.js";

// ✅ Correct - handles long content automatically
addLongField(embed, "📦 Items", itemList);

// ❌ Wrong - will crash if itemList exceeds 1024 chars
embed.addFields({ name: "📦 Items", value: itemList });
```

This applies to any command that displays lists, inventories, or other variable-length content in embed fields.
